A||||2||CountFiero||Timing gear installation Which One First ????||||5||
Z||000000||CountFiero||11-29-2001||06:48 PM||||I am in the Midst of the DREADED timing gear replacement.  I got everything off OK now it's time to install the NEW gears.  But here's the question---Which gear goes on first?  OR do they have to be "meshed" and installed together??  I should add that this is my 4cyl 2.5 engine ( I bet the 6 is alot easier).<BR>I already know the proceedure for pressing the timing gear on using a bolt and washer and nut to "press/pull" it on with the center of the cam shaft threaded.  <BR>BUT, Do I press the timing gear on FIRST and then try to install the crankshaft gear AFTER or at the same time, or WHAT?<BR>Suggestions??? Tricks??? Any advice from someone who has done this before is welcome.<BR>Thanks in advance to everyone!!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||11-29-2001||07:44 PM||||Install the crank gear first and line the timing marks will mesh and install the camshaft.||||reg||1
Z||000002||ITB 2M4||11-29-2001||11:58 PM||||Just like IRG said above. If you have the metal ones, there should be a dot on each gear.  Make sure they line up when installed.  I havn't ever installed the stock fiber gear, so I don't know about that one.<P>------------------<BR>SCCA ITB '84 Fiero 2M4||||reg||1
